Somebody suggested a while ago that in Wizard mode, one should be able to
request special levels (ones with shops, zoos, etc.). I believe it was also
suggested that one should be able to create fountains, thrones, etc.

It seems to me that what is really needed is a complete level-editor for
nethack. Also, there should be some way of saving levels, or sets of levels,
so that other people could play them as a "programmed adventure."

Right now, the only way I know of for accomplishing anything like the above
(for non-programmers, that is) is to go into Wizard mode, create lots of
interesting monsters and treasure on a level, then kill yourself and save
the bones file. The main problems with this method are 1) that it is limited
in scope of design (you can't create thrones, etc), and 2) that you can't
guarantee that the next player will hit the bones level.

With a real level-editor, and enough willing dungeon-designers, the scope
of nethack could be greatly increased.


